The copy constructor is already minimal. Each member is copied directly through the initializer list, and the base class copies its own data. I found no change that would make it measurably faster without risking different behavior. The only difference below is that the base-class copy now uses an explicit `static_cast<const FieldBase&>`. That is semantically identical, so behavior is unchanged, and I don't expect it to change speed.

```cpp
Field::Field(const Field &field)
    : FieldBase(static_cast<const FieldBase &>(field))
    , profile(field.profile)
    , profileIndex(field.profileIndex)
    , type(field.type)
    , isFieldExpanded(field.isFieldExpanded)
{
}
```